// T11 — What Sift decided reaches Moment and Trace
// Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md ("S:n" = its line n) and the accepted ADRs docs/adrs/SIFT-ADR-0*.md.
// Founder ruling 2026-11-04: Source = "Spec of record". NDD-SOURCE section 6 gives thread structure and titles only; where it differs from the spec, the spec wins.
//
// STORY FLOW (founder ruling bd996f3e, 2026-11-07, "15 story flows, branches inside"): the main path runs from the start of the thread to its T11.O11 terminal, in the order the spec tells it.
// Every alternative of the thread, once a flow of its own, is a branch at the moment where it diverges: a [branch] moment that holds its deciding event as a plain node (moved from the main path, not copied), an empty first arm `TheMainPath` (the walk takes the first arm when none is chosen, so the main path is the one that goes on after the moment) and one `when` arm for each alternative,
// each ending at its own exit ([outcome] when it is a normal outcome of the thread, [terminal] for a failure or a refusal) or falling through into the moments that follow. Moment derives one scenario for each path. A refusal is a precondition of a command; Moment 0.9.0 derives its negative scenario for every path of the flow (ADR-042). A branch moment that nothing precedes (the first node of the flow, or one whose deciding event is the only node of the previous branch moment's main arm) keeps its first arm `TheMainPath` with the main path's next nodes: no event to anchor on (docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md, 0.9.0 rework).
// A branch arm cites the former flow it carries in its first comment line (the old-to-new mapping is in docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md).
// BRANCHES:
// DIFFERENCE FROM NDD-SOURCE (spec wins): T11.M2·B1 (no entitlement or a bad token) and T11.N1 are not drawn: the spec gives Sift no such refusal
//   (S:278; HALT-8 of the contexts rework), so the arm was a minted code.
// carried from the former main flow, its description: description "T11 — What Sift decided reaches Moment and Trace (O11). Context lane: C3 Design Model (the emitted Cycle). Spec of record: S:900-911 Sagas and Cycle records. The Cycle records are process events of the Cycle; the consumer is an external lane."
// Part of the model directory; validate with `moment parse model/` (project mode) and `moment test` on this file.

flow "T11 — What Sift decided reaches Moment and Trace"
  description "T11 — What Sift decided reaches Moment and Trace. The story of the thread from its start to its T11.O11 outcome, with its alternatives as branches at the moment where each diverges. Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md."

  lane design "DesignModel" [Core]
  lane enablement "Enablement" [Supporting]
  lane consumers "Consumers" [External]

  moment "T11.M1 · Every write is emitted after it is made"
    design: StartCycle  // S:958 "StartCycle(trigger: CycleTrigger, decision: RecordRef, attempt, redrives?, replayPoint?, endPoint?);"
    design: CycleStarted  // S:902 "**StartCycle**(trigger: CycleTrigger, decision: RecordRef, attempt, redrives?, replayPoint?, endPoint?) (NEW) records **CycleStarted** {CycleId, trigger: CycleTrigger, decision: RecordRef, attempt, redrives?, replayPoint?, endPoint?} first, for every Cycle that starts."
    design: ConstructAliased  // S:616,621 every Lineage event is a write the Cycle emits as NodeChanged
    design: ConstructRenamed  // S:617,621
    design: ConstructMoved  // S:618,621
    design: ConstructRetyped  // S:619,621
    design: SupersessionRefused  // S:620,621 a Lineage event too: emitted as NodeChanged like the other four
    design: RecordNodeChange  // S:903 "RecordNodeChange(write Pointer or RecordRef, CycleId) (NEW) records NodeChanged"
    design: NodeChanged  // S:902 "Each write is emitted as **NodeChanged** {the write's Pointer, or its RecordRef for a SequenceRecords write (§8), CycleId}, recorded by RecordNodeChange (next bullet)."
    // Emitted events carry Pointers, not content (S:632 and ADR-084). The five Lineage events above are the writes this moment emits; they are the Lineage events the spec names (S:620, S:632).
    // Their commands and the other writes of a Cycle belong to T3, T4, T13 and T14.

  moment "T11.M2 · A consumer subscribes"
    note consumers: "A consumer subscribes to the emitted Cycle: the management API's read side is a subscription to the emitted Cycle and a query by position, no other reads. The mechanism is SIFT-ADR-084; the API is OAuth2 and the spec gives Sift no refusal for a missing entitlement or a bad token"  // S:278 "one read side for consumers of the emitted Cycle"

  moment "T11.M3 · A consumer catches up and goes live"
    note consumers: "The consumer catches up by a query by position and then goes live on the subscription (the management API's read side is a subscription and a query by position)"  // S:278 "a query by position"

  moment "T11.M4 · It sees a failure"
    design: RecordStepFailure  // S:960 "RecordStepFailure(step?, reason codes, Pointers);"
    design: SagaStepFailed  // S:926 "A failed attempt: RecordStepFailure (NEW), issued by the executor when a step fails after its brief retries, records SagaStepFailed before CompleteCycle records CycleCompleted{Failed}"
    design: CompleteCycle  // S:959 "CompleteCycle(outcome, failedCommands?, ingressEffect?, constructStates, designState, position);"
    design: CycleCompleted  // S:905 "**CycleCompleted** {outcome: Succeeded | Failed"
    // Failed: designState is open, constructStates is [] and position is the last write; no query runs, so a Failed end can't itself fail (S:909).

  moment "T11.M4 · Then the success"
    // Subscribers can see CycleCompleted{Failed} and then {Succeeded} for the same trigger, with distinct attempts (S:909).
    design: CompleteCycle  // S:959 "CompleteCycle(outcome, failedCommands?, ingressEffect?, constructStates, designState, position);"
    design: CycleCompleted  // S:909 "**Subscribers can see CycleCompleted{Failed} and then {Succeeded}** for the same trigger"
    // DIFFERENCE FROM NDD-SOURCE (spec wins): the node `enablement: SetupCompleted` is kept. NDD lists only lane C3 for this moment; the spec names
    // SetupCompleted as the record that the read models exist (S:907), so the C1 event is the real construct here (audit C-52).

  moment "T11.M5 · It reads the design state"
    enablement: SetupCompleted  // S:907 constructStates and designState are read "whenever the read models exist": the current key generation's read models are built (a SetupCompleted records it)
    // Otherwise (never enabled, retired or destroyed) and for every retention and License-scope Cycle: designState open, constructStates [], position
    // its last write (S:907). designState is SystemValidated only under the verdict rule of Assessment (S:907; T10.M5).

  moment "T11.O11 · The decisions reached the consumers (terminal)"
    design: PassCompleted [terminal]  // S:675,895 the verdict that CycleCompleted.designState reads
    // PROVES: CycleStarted -> NodeChanged* -> CycleCompleted visible to a subscribed consumer, and the same events by query from any position; Pointers and identifiers only (S:902-905, ADR-084).
    // The terminal node is the one declared construct the spec ties to CycleCompleted: the verdict that decides designState (S:907).
